  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">R&#xE9;ponse rapide &#xE0; l&#x2019;&#xE9;pid&#xE9;mie de chol&#xE9;ra dans la province du Sankuru et dans les hotspot de la R&#xE9;publique D&#xE9;mocratique du Congo</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this project is to provide water, sanitation and hygiene assistance to communities affected by, and those at risk of, cholera in Sankuru, Sud Kivu and Tanganyika provinces. This UNICEF project reinforces disease surveillance and early case detection, implements the case-area targeted intervention (CATI) approach to contain the outbreak, and raises community awareness about appropriate hygiene practices. The project provides humanitarian assistance to 175,000 people, including 31,000 women, 25,000 men, 119,000 children, and including 26,000 persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
